Automatic tests for Runtime Resource Overlay (RRO)


Host side:

- run.sh
    Entry point for host side interaction with tests. Execute 'run.sh -r' to
    build, sync and run all tests, or 'run -h' for a full list of options.


Device side:

The test suite is installed in /data/nativetest/rro_tests along with auxiliary
data (i.e. a bunch of apks).

- RROBase.cpp
    Base class for all RRO tests. Contains common helper functions.

- RRONativeTests.cpp
    Tests running exclusively in native. Quick to run. Verifies the actual
    RRO mechanism. If the native tests do not pass, neither will the Java
    tests.

- RROJavaTests.cpp
    Tests implemented in Java. Takes a few minutes to run. Verifies that the
    Android framework correctly loads both target and overlay packages.

    The Java tests work with three configurations of overlay packages. The
    configurations are Setup0 (no overlays), Setup1 (one overlay) and Setup2
    (two overlays).

    The Java tests follow this outline:

    - Android is stopped ('stop').

    - The file system is populated with a suitable set of overlays (copied from
      /data/nativetests/rro_tests/data).

    - Android is started ('start').

    - The Java instrumentation tests are executed ('am instrument -e setup X').
      The currently used setup is passed as a parameter, and will be read in
      Java by inspecting getArguments().

    - The instrumentation output is parsed.

    - Android is stopped ('stop').

    - The test overlays are removed.

    - Android is started ('start').
